187 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 54 0 R/T(For the eight test cases above, both implementations give the intended policy outcome. The separate-if version returns a list because it can collect multiple decisions; the chained version returns one decision string. To expose the risk of overlapping independent conditions, a poorly written implementation such as `if units <= 200` followed by `if units >= 100` would execute both blocks for values from 100 through 200.)/E(For the eight test cases above, both implementations give the intended policy outcome. The separate-if version returns a list because it can collect multiple decisions; the chained version returns one decision string. To expose the risk of overlapping independent conditions, a poorly written implementation such as `if units <= 200` followed by `if units >= 100` would execute both blocks for values from 100 through 200.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[39]>>
endobj

188 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 54 0 R/T(1.4 Design decision and alternative)/E(1.4 Design decision and alternative)/Pg 12 0 R/K[40]>>
endobj

189 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 54 0 R/T(Combined Boolean conditions are appropriate for the slab boundaries because each rule can be read in one line using chained comparisons and `and`. A small nested if is useful after selecting the 101\205200 or above-200 band, because the eligibility detail is then checked only within that band. This structure is easy to modify without duplicating the range conditions.)/E(Combined Boolean conditions are appropriate for the slab boundaries because each rule can be read in one line using chained comparisons and `and`. A small nested if is useful after selecting the 101\205200 or above-200 band, because the eligibility detail is then checked only within that band. This structure is easy to modify without duplicating the range conditions.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[41]>>
endobj

190 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 54 0 R/T(A Python 3.10+ match\205case alternative can match on a category computed from the units, then check the extra eligibility condition. A list of upper-limit/decision pairs can also be scanned in order. With k slabs, an ordered list scan takes O\(k\) time in the worst case and O\(k\) space for the stored rules. An if\205elif chain takes O\(k\) worst-case checks and O\(1\) extra space; match\205case has O\(k\) worst-case matching in this simple case and O\(1\) extra space. For a fixed small number of slabs, all are effectively constant-sized; the chain is clearest here.)/E(A Python 3.10+ match\205case alternative can match on a category computed from the units, then check the extra eligibility condition. A list of upper-limit/decision pairs can also be scanned in order. With k slabs, an ordered list scan takes O\(k\) time in the worst case and O\(k\) space for the stored rules. An if\205elif chain takes O\(k\) worst-case checks and O\(1\) extra space; match\205case has O\(k\) worst-case matching in this simple case and O\(1\) extra space. For a fixed small number of slabs, all are effectively constant-sized; the chain is clearest here.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[42]>>
endobj

191 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 54 0 R/T(2.1 While-loop design)/E(2.1 While-loop design)/Pg 12 0 R/K[43]>>
endobj

192 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 54 0 R/T( Q2 \205 LOOPS THAT COUNT ATTEMPTS)/E( Q2 \205 LOOPS THAT COUNT ATTEMPTS)/Pg 12 0 R/K[44]>>
endobj

193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 54 0 R/Pg 12 0 R/A[567 0 R 0]/K[45]>>
endobj

194 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(The for-loop version has a subtle issue if blank entries should not count: `range\(3\)` counts loop iterations, including blank entries. A robust version must use a while loop, or use a separate counted-attempt loop that repeats blank entries without consuming one of the three wrong attempts. For this requirement, the while loop directly models the number of counted attempts and is therefore the more natural design.)/E(The for-loop version has a subtle issue if blank entries should not count: `range\(3\)` counts loop iterations, including blank entries. A robust version must use a while loop, or use a separate counted-attempt loop that repeats blank entries without consuming one of the three wrong attempts. For this requirement, the while loop directly models the number of counted attempts and is therefore the more natural design.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

195 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 55 0 R/T(2.3 Changed condition: two extra attempts after security answer)/E(2.3 Changed condition: two extra attempts after security answer)/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

196 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(After the customer correctly answers the security question, the maximum number of counted OTP attempts becomes five; otherwise it remains three. The maximum can be set before entering the loop. Blank entries still do not increment the counter.)/E(After the customer correctly answers the security question, the maximum number of counted OTP attempts becomes five; otherwise it remains three. The maximum can be set before entering the loop. Blank entries still do not increment the counter.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

197 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 55 0 R/T(A recursive function could receive the remaining attempt count and call itself after a wrong nonblank entry. Each counted attempt performs O\(1\) work, so total time is O\(a\) for a attempts. A loop uses O\(1\) auxiliary space. Recursion uses O\(a\) call-stack space and is less suitable for a small bounded retry process. A counter updated before checking for a blank input can incorrectly consume attempts; a counter never updated after a wrong input can create an infinite loop.)/E(A recursive function could receive the remaining attempt count and call itself after a wrong nonblank entry. Each counted attempt performs O\(1\) work, so total time is O\(a\) for a attempts. A loop uses O\(1\) auxiliary space. Recursion uses O\(a\) call-stack space and is less suitable for a small bounded retry process. A counter updated before checking for a blank input can incorrectly consume attempts; a counter never updated after a wrong input can create an infinite loop.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

198 0 obj
