333 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 59 0 R/T(Writing each line directly to a file avoids retaining the entire statement in RAM. `io.StringIO` provides an in- memory text buffer with a file-like write interface. Both approaches process n lines in O\(n\) time; file streaming uses O\(1\) application-level buffering \(excluding operating-system buffers\), while StringIO and join retain O\(N\) output storage. Repeated += may have O\(N\262\) copying in the worst case. Use join when the complete result is needed in memory, and streaming when the output is large and can be written incrementally.)/E(Writing each line directly to a file avoids retaining the entire statement in RAM. `io.StringIO` provides an in- memory text buffer with a file-like write interface. Both approaches process n lines in O\(n\) time; file streaming uses O\(1\) application-level buffering \(excluding operating-system buffers\), while StringIO and join retain O\(N\) output storage. Repeated += may have O\(N\262\) copying in the worst case. Use join when the complete result is needed in memory, and streaming when the output is large and can be written incrementally.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 59 0 R/T(Q5 \205 FUNCTIONS, PARAMETERS AND SCOPE)/E(Q5 \205 FUNCTIONS, PARAMETERS AND SCOPE)/Pg 17 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

335 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 59 0 R/T(In `def add_item\(item, order=[]\)`, the empty list is created once when the function is defined. Every call that omits `order` refers to that same list. Appending for one customer therefore changes the default list seen by the next customer. The safe pattern is to use None as the default and create a fresh list inside the function.)/E(In `def add_item\(item, order=[]\)`, the empty list is created once when the function is defined. Every call that omits `order` refers to that same list. Appending for one customer therefore changes the default list seen by the next customer. The safe pattern is to use None as the default and create a fresh list inside the function.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

336 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 59 0 R/T(Positional parameters are concise when the argument order is obvious, such as `add_item\("Tea", order\)`. Keyword parameters improve clarity when there are several options, such as `calculate_bill\(items, gst_rate=0.05\)`. Default parameters are suitable for optional values that are safe to share, such as immutable numbers or strings; mutable lists should generally use None. Python can return multiple values as a tuple.)/E(Positional parameters are concise when the argument order is obvious, such as `add_item\("Tea", order\)`. Keyword parameters improve clarity when there are several options, such as `calculate_bill\(items, gst_rate=0.05\)`. Default parameters are suitable for optional values that are safe to share, such as immutable numbers or strings; mutable lists should generally use None. Python can return multiple values as a tuple.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

