387 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 60 0 R/T(The caller can always pass a fresh list explicitly, which makes ownership clear but requires every caller to construct the list. A closure can keep a private order list inside a function that returns an inner add function; this is useful when a persistent order object is intended. Appending one item to a Python list is amortised O\(1\) time. Each customer\220s order requires O\(m\) space for m stored items. The None-default design is simple and keeps each call independent.)/E(The caller can always pass a fresh list explicitly, which makes ownership clear but requires every caller to construct the list. A closure can keep a private order list inside a function that returns an inner add function; this is useful when a persistent order object is intended. Appending one item to a Python list is amortised O\(1\) time. Each customer\220s order requires O\(m\) space for m stored items. The None-default design is simple and keeps each call independent.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

