397 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 61 0 R/T(For n=5, the naive call tree begins with W\(5\) calling W\(4\) and W\(3\). W\(4\) calls W\(3\) and W\(2\); the separate W\(3\) branch calls W\(2\) and W\(1\). The same subproblems \(W\(3\), W\(2\), and W\(1\)\) are recalculated repeatedly. This repeated work causes exponential growth.)/E(For n=5, the naive call tree begins with W\(5\) calling W\(4\) and W\(3\). W\(4\) calls W\(3\) and W\(2\); the separate W\(3\) branch calls W\(2\) and W\(1\). The same subproblems \(W\(3\), W\(2\), and W\(1\)\) are recalculated repeatedly. This repeated work causes exponential growth.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

