<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 64 0 R/T(The naive recursive algorithm repeats the same subproblems. Each call for n greater than 1 launches two more calls, and the call tree expands rapidly. The measured call count for n=25 is 242,785, while memoisation needs only 26 function evaluations. The dominant cost is not the addition itself; it is repeated evaluation of identical W\(k\) values.)/E(The naive recursive algorithm repeats the same subproblems. Each call for n greater than 1 launches two more calls, and the call tree expands rapidly. The measured call count for n=25 is 242,785, while memoisation needs only 26 function evaluations. The dominant cost is not the addition itself; it is repeated evaluation of identical W\(k\) values.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
