793 0 obj
<</Title(1.3 Implementations)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 629 0 R/Prev 853 0 R/First 854 0 R/Last 854 0 R/Count -1/Next 734 0 R>>
endobj

794 0 obj
<</Title(Combined Boolean conditions are appropriate for the slab boundaries because each rule can be read in one line using chained comparisons and `and`. A small nested if is useful after selecting the 101\205200 or above-200 band, because the eligibility detail is then checked only within that band. This structure is easy to modify without duplicating the range conditions.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 734 0 R/Next 795 0 R>>
endobj

795 0 obj
<</Title(A Python 3.10+ match\205case alternative can match on a category computed from the units, then check the extra eligibility condition. A list of upper-limit/decision pairs can also be scanned in order. With k slabs, an ordered list scan takes O\(k\) time in the worst case and O\(k\) space for the stored rules. An if\205elif chain takes O\(k\) worst-case checks and O\(1\) extra space; match\205case has O\(k\) worst-case matching in this simple case and O\(1\) extra space. For a fixed small number of slabs, all are effectively constant-sized; the chain is clearest here.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 734 0 R/Prev 794 0 R>>
endobj

796 0 obj
<</Title(2.1 While-loop design)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 735 0 R/Next 797 0 R>>
endobj

797 0 obj
<</Title(A blank entry uses continue before the counter is increased, so it does not consume an attempt. A correct OTP uses break to leave the loop immediately. The loop\220s else clause runs only when the loop finishes normally because its condition becomes false; it is skipped when break executes. The `pass` statement is a no-operation placeholder and is not logically required for this solution. It can be demonstrated in a branch reserved for a future audit action.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 735 0 R/Prev 796 0 R>>
endobj

798 0 obj
<</Title(2.2 For-loop design)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 735 0 R/First 855 0 R/Last 855 0 R/Count -1/Next 856 0 R>>
endobj

799 0 obj
<</Title(Q6 \205 RECURSION AND ITS LIMITS)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 857 0 R/First 858 0 R/Last 859 0 R/Count -3/Next 736 0 R>>
endobj

800 0 obj
<</Title(Ways)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 736 0 R/Next 860 0 R>>
endobj

801 0 obj
<</Title(For n=25, the expected values are 121,393 ways, 242,785 naive calls and 26 memoised calls. The memoised function evaluates each distinct n value once, so the number of function evaluations is linear in n. The naive call count grows exponentially.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 736 0 R/Prev 861 0 R>>
endobj

