<</Title(5.4 Three-customer independence test)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 878 0 R/Next 857 0 R>>
endobj

868 0 obj
<</Title(The caller can always pass a fresh list explicitly, which makes ownership clear but requires every caller to construct the list. A closure can keep a private order list inside a function that returns an inner add function; this is useful when a persistent order object is intended. Appending one item to a Python list is amortised O\(1\) time. Each customer\220s order requires O\(m\) space for m stored items. The None-default design is simple and keeps each call independent.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 857 0 R>>
endobj

