879 0 obj
<</Title(Let W\(n\) be the number of ways to climb n steps using 1-step or 2-step moves. The final move must come from either step n\2121 or step n\2122, so W\(n\) = W\(n\2121\) + W\(n\2122\). The base cases are W\(0\)=1 and W\(1\)=1. The supplied code uses `n <= 1` returning 1, which is equivalent for the requested nonnegative inputs.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 869 0 R>>
endobj

880 0 obj
<</Title(For n=5, the naive call tree begins with W\(5\) calling W\(4\) and W\(3\). W\(4\) calls W\(3\) and W\(2\); the separate W\(3\) branch calls W\(2\) and W\(1\). The same subproblems \(W\(3\), W\(2\), and W\(1\)\) are recalculated repeatedly. This repeated work causes exponential growth.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 859 0 R/Prev 870 0 R/First 893 0 R/Last 894 0 R/Count -3/Next 895 0 R>>
endobj

