892 0 obj
<</Title(A local name exists inside its function. A global name is defined at module level. A nonlocal name belongs to an enclosing function scope and can be rebound from an inner function. Reading a global name is allowed, but assigning to it inside a function makes Python treat that name as local unless `global` is declared. Global mutation is usually avoided because it creates hidden dependencies and makes testing harder; passing values as arguments and returning results is clearer.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 878 0 R/Prev 912 0 R>>
endobj

