endobj

928 0 obj
<</Title(Writing each line directly to a file avoids retaining the entire statement in RAM. `io.StringIO` provides an in- memory text buffer with a file-like write interface. Both approaches process n lines in O\(n\) time; file streaming uses O\(1\) application-level buffering \(excluding operating-system buffers\), while StringIO and join retain O\(N\) output storage. Repeated += may have O\(N\262\) copying in the worst case. Use join when the complete result is needed in memory, and streaming when the output is large and can be written incrementally.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 910 0 R>>
endobj

929 0 obj
<</Title(In `def add_item\(item, order=[]\)`, the empty list is created once when the function is defined. Every call that omits `order` refers to that same list. Appending for one customer therefore changes the default list seen by the next customer. The safe pattern is to use None as the default and create a fresh list inside the function.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 911 0 R/Next 930 0 R>>
endobj

930 0 obj
<</Title(Expected behaviour: the two buggy calls both display the shared list containing Tea and Vada. The corrected calls display independent one-item lists. `add_item_buggy.__defaults__` displays a tuple containing the default list object; after the calls, that list contains the appended items.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 911 0 R/Prev 929 0 R>>
endobj

