955 0 obj
<</Title(The expected best general-purpose approach is join\(\). Strings are immutable, so concatenation conceptually creates new string objects. Repeatedly extending a growing string can cause previously accumulated characters to be copied again, producing up to O\(N\262\) character-copying work in an unfavourable implementation. `join\(\)` first receives the pieces and creates the combined string in one operation, giving O\(N\) time in the total output length. CPython can optimise some `+=` patterns, but that behaviour is an implementation detail and should not be relied on as a portable design guarantee.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 941 0 R>>
endobj

